      "message": "Done. I initially assumed `bounds()` had to return the shape in its local coordinates but your explanation makes a lot of sense. I made this here return `maskBounds()` which makes it a bit more clear that `Geometry::bounds()` can have a different meaning for different kinds of geometry.",
